<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Optional DAB-only layout for skin authors. Copy the screen into your skin XML.
This example is not loaded automatically and does not change the default UI.

DabRdsDisplay is used only for DAB services (4115), both satellite and SDR.
DVB radio continues to use RdsDisplay or the existing RdsInfoDisplay layout.
Without DabRdsDisplay, DAB also uses that common radio fallback. Use the name
RdsDisplay instead if you intentionally want the same layout for all radio.
No Python class or callback is renamed. The layout changes on service start,
not on each metadata update. Both optional names opt into skin-owned colors
and transparency even without DabImage.
Custom layouts are hidden on TV/service stop and shown again on radio.

Adding DabImage opts into a skin-owned DAB image layout: Enigma2 preserves
the widget position/size and the RDS screen/text colors and transparency.
The built-in DAB radio cabinet is not drawn in this mode. Place your own
artwork with normal ePixmap elements if desired. A black GUI background
remains underneath, so no video decoder is needed for PCM radio playback.

DabImage shows the received slideshow, or the default DAB logo when no
slide is available or the slideshow is disabled (if radio backgrounds are
enabled). A skin may provide icons/default_dab.png to replace that logo.
Without DabImage, the existing default radio/slideshow layout is retained.

Keep RadioText, RtpText and RassLogo in the screen. Image coordinates are
relative to the screen; the complete image must fit inside its bounds.
The resolution attribute lets the skin engine scale this HD example to
FHD. Use a 4:3 image area and centerScaled to preserve slide proportions.
RadioText/RtpText support explicit fontScale or scrollText attributes.

The optional technical status line and front-panel display mode remain
controlled by DAB settings. Disable the automatic technical line if your
skin provides its own ServiceInfo/DABTechnical widget.

Additional ServiceInfo converters for session.CurrentService:
  DABCodec       - transmitted AAC-LC, HE-AAC, HE-AAC v2 or MPEG Layer II
  DABSampleRate  - audio rate after SBR, e.g. "48 kHz" (value: Hz, -1 unknown)
  DABChannelMode - translated Mono/Stereo/Joint stereo/Dual channel/Surround
  DABStereo      - boolean for a stereo icon; text is the same channel mode
Rate and mode stay empty until detected. PS reconstructs stereo from a mono
AAC core; forcing PCM output does not change the displayed source format.
DABStereo is false for mono, dual channel, surround and unknown formats.
Use render="Label" for text, or ConditionalShowHide with DABStereo for icons.
These fields use existing service events; they do not poll the tuner.
SDR requires the welle-cli source-format reporting patch (r9).

Broadcast RASS, DVB radio and audio decoding are not changed by this skin.
-->
<skin>
	<screen name="DabRdsDisplay" position="0,0" size="1280,720" resolution="1280,720" zPosition="-2" backgroundColor="#FF000000" flags="wfNoBorder">
		<widget source="session.CurrentService" render="Label" position="60,25" size="1160,45" font="Regular;32" foregroundColor="#00ffffff" backgroundColor="#00121922" transparent="1" halign="center" noWrap="1">
			<convert type="ServiceName">Name</convert>
		</widget>
		<widget name="DabImage" position="320,90" size="640,480" alphatest="blend" scaleFlags="centerScaled" />
		<widget name="RadioText" position="60,590" size="1160,45" font="Regular;30" foregroundColor="#00ffffff" backgroundColor="#00121922" transparent="1" halign="center" valign="center" noWrap="1" />
		<widget name="RtpText" position="60,645" size="1160,35" font="Regular;23" foregroundColor="#00a8c6d8" backgroundColor="#00121922" transparent="1" halign="center" valign="center" noWrap="1" />
		<widget name="RassLogo" pixmap="icons/rass_logo.png" position="60,90" size="50,21" alphatest="blend" />
	</screen>
</skin>
